<h2 id="org46ceba4"><span class="section-number-2">1</span> About</h2>
<div class="outline-text-2" id="text-1">
<p>
This document it's aimed to help to configure <b>mostly any</b> <i>Ubuntu</i>
(and recently <i>Fedora</i>) distro to working-distro with the most
common set-up that I'm used to.  The distro-dependency is because
this includes some package-managers-dependency, I include on the
codes some scripting in shell for invoquing the installation.  Main
tools, corporate and productivity tools; and of course with the
look&amp;feel from a preconfigured repo.
</p>

<p>
Following literate documentation approach, inspiring post:
<a href="http://cachestocaches.com/2018/6/org-literate-programming/">http://cachestocaches.com/2018/6/org-literate-programming/</a>
</p>

<blockquote>
<p>

All the shell code here comes without any warranty, AT ALL,
execute it (or not) at your own risk.  I assume that you
understand the code, you can modif, use it, post it, or whatever,
at your own risk :)
</p>
</blockquote>

<p>
Also, document format for exporting in HTML is from <a href="https://gongzhitaao.org/orgcss/">gongzhitaao</a>,
