<div id="outline-container-orga0f683d" class="outline-4">
<h4 id="orga0f683d"><span class="section-number-4">4.3.1</span> Pokemon on your terminal</h4>
<div class="outline-text-4" id="text-4-3-1">
<p>
I love the pokemon say addon for terminal, is a litle bit of fun on
your term:
</p>

<ul class="org-ul">
<li><a href="https://github.com/possatti/pokemonsay">https://github.com/possatti/pokemonsay</a></li>
</ul>

<div class="org-src-container">
<pre class="src src-sh">
sudo apt-get install fortune cowsay

</pre>
</div>

<p>
For Fedora, there is an slight difference
</p>

<div class="org-src-container">
<pre class="src src-sh">
sudo dnf install fortune-mod
sudo dnf install cowsay

</pre>
</div>

<p>
Some test that you have preinstalled what is needed:
</p>

<div class="org-src-container">
<pre class="src src-sh">
fortune | cowsay

</pre>
</div>

<div class="org-src-container">
<pre class="src src-sh">
cd ~/
git clone http://github.com/possatti/pokemonsay
cd pokemonsay
./install.sh

</pre>
</div>

<p>
Now you want to add it to your .bashrc file to get some cool wellcome everytime you enter to your terminal.
</p>

<div class="org-src-container">
<pre class="src src-sh">
cp ~/.bashrc ~/.bashrc.before.pokesay
echo "# Pokemon say add-on" &gt;&gt; ~/.bashrc
echo "fortune | ~/bin/pokemonsay " &gt;&gt; ~/.bashrc
diff ~/.bashrc ~/.bashrc.before.pokesay

</pre>
</div>
