</div>
<div id="outline-container-orgc7db448" class="outline-3">
<h3 id="orgc7db448"><span class="section-number-3">7.1</span> GDM - Fedora login screen background</h3>
<div class="outline-text-3" id="text-7-1">
<p>
This should be easy but isn't&#x2026; something quite simple like
changing the user's login background it is a little big triky.
</p>

<p>
For being able to modify the Gnome Desktop Manager login screen
background you will need to download an specific application.
</p>

<p>
Here is what I found in
<a href="https://copr.fedorainfracloud.org/coprs/zirix/gdm-wallpaper/">https://copr.fedorainfracloud.org/coprs/zirix/gdm-wallpaper/</a>
</p>

<div class="org-src-container">
<pre class="src src-sh">
sudo dnf copr enable zirix/gdm-wallpaper
sudo dnf install gdm-wallpaper
sudo set-gdm-wallpaper /path/to/image.png

</pre>
</div>

<p>
And works! I disabled the repository added just in case once is
installed.
</p>
</div>
</div>

<div id="outline-container-org7bbe94d" class="outline-3">
