<div id="outline-container-org6e409dc" class="outline-3">
<h3 id="org6e409dc"><span class="section-number-3">7.3</span> xmonad tiling windows manager</h3>
<div class="outline-text-3" id="text-7-3">
<p>
I've tried Xmonad and has that minimilistic touch that I love, so
this is an option to take into consideration, heres is how to
install.
</p>

<p>
The following is for install For Fedora:
</p>

<div class="org-src-container">
<pre class="src src-sh">
sudo dnf install xmonad

</pre>
</div>

<p>
I use xmobar with xmonad, so let's install it:
</p>

<div class="org-src-container">
<pre class="src src-sh">
sudo dnf install xmobar

</pre>
</div>

<p>
For easy the configuration you have .xmonad and .xmobarrc inside
<b>dotfiles</b>
</p>

<div class="org-src-container">
<pre class="src src-sh">
printf "Check config and other scripts used by Xmonad and Xmobar:\n\n"
ls -l dotfiles/.xmo*

</pre>
</div>

<p>
Here is the configuration for xmobar
</p>

<div class="org-src-container">
<pre class="src src-sh">
cat dotfiles/.xmobarrc

</pre>
</div>
</div>
